  "presentation_summary": [
    "55-year-old man with chronic heart failure medications presented with progressive fatigue on minimal exertion, weight loss, diarrhea, heat intolerance, hypersudoresis, palpitations, dyspnea on exertion, retrosternal tightness, leg edema, and abdominal distension.",
    "He denied fever, tremor, and abdominal pain; he was afebrile with blood pressure 120/61 mmHg and heart rate 115/min on room air.",
    "Examination showed sarcopenia, dehydration, icteric sclerae, jugular venous engorgement, ascites, and bilateral pitting edema.",
    "Initial labs showed hemoglobin 4.1 g/dL, total bilirubin 14.62 mg/dL, direct bilirubin 11.22 mg/dL, INR 1.35, NT-proBNP 10236 pg/mL, TSH 0.010 uU/mL, fT3 10.30 pg/mL, fT4 7.27 ng/dL, and TRAb 160.",
    "Echocardiography showed diffuse LV hypokinesia, marked biatrial dilation, severe aortic/mitral/tricuspid regurgitation, and PASP 36 mmHg; thyroid ultrasound later showed an enlarged hypervascular heterogeneous thyroid."
  ],
